<title>ITALY: Italy's Trieste sees Dec CPI at 2.8 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Trieste sees Dec CPI at 2.8 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TRIESTE, Italy 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Trieste said its December consumer price index stood at 0.2 percent month-on-month and 2.8 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In November, Trieste's inflation rate was 0.3 percent and 2.6 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Trieste is one of 10 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 2.49 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to November 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.2   (0.3)     2.8  (2.6)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.3   (0.1)     3.5  (3.3)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.1   (0.1)     3.4  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.0   (0.6)     4.8  (5.0)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.1   (0.1)     2.9  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.0   (0.0)     1.5  (1.5)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.2   (1.0)     3.0  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.2   (0.5)     3.2  (3.1)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.0   (3.6)     6.2  (6.6)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0   (0.0)     3.9  (3.9)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0   (0.1)    -0.7 (-0.7)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
